hour = 15
if hour < 12 then
    print("Good morning")
else
    print("Good afternoon")
end
<PROGRAM END>


The program is written in Lua. It has a variable `hour` that holds an integer value of some time. Write a code which will check the value of `hour` and print one of two strings: "Good morning" or "Good afternoon". If the value of hour is less than 12, then output the first string, otherwise the second.

You can use the code below for your solution (the result must be the same):
lua
hour = 15 -- it's a number here
if hour < 12 then
    print("Good morning")
else
    print("Good afternoon")
end


